#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:717
#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1770
msgid "What Authlify does"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:717
msgid "One plugin that protects the WordPress login, lets people prove who they are, and makes the login page look like your site."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:719
msgid "Authlify replaces several single-purpose login plugins. Everything below is in the free plugin, with no limits and no license."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:721
msgid "<strong>A private login address.</strong> Move wp-login.php to an address only you know. Bots that request wp-login.php or /wp-admin/ get a normal “page not found”."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:722
msgid "<strong>Brute-force lockouts.</strong> An address that keeps guessing passwords has to wait, and the wait grows each time."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:723
msgid "<strong>CAPTCHA and a honeypot.</strong> Cloudflare Turnstile, hCaptcha, Google reCAPTCHA or the self-hosted ALTCHA, on WordPress and WooCommerce forms."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:724
msgid "<strong>Two-factor login and passkeys.</strong> Authenticator apps, backup codes, passkeys and hardware keys, set up by each person from their profile."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:725
msgid "<strong>Breached-password check.</strong> Refuse new passwords that appear in known data breaches (opt-in)."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:726
msgid "<strong>Hardening.</strong> XML-RPC, application passwords, username discovery, vague login errors and a private-site mode."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:727
msgid "<strong>Activity log.</strong> Logins, failed attempts and lockouts, stored only in your database."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:728
msgid "<strong>Login page designer.</strong> Templates, “Match my site”, and every login screen styled in one place."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:729
msgid "<strong>Leak Check.</strong> Probes your own site from the outside to prove the hidden login address does not leak."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:731
#, php-format
msgid "Authlify was called Modify Login before version 3.0. Upgraded sites keep their login address and settings; see %s."
msgstr ""

