#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:748
msgid "What activation changes"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:749
msgid "On a new site, nothing about how people log in changes yet: the login page stays at wp-login.php until you choose a new address. Brute-force lockouts, the activity log and the weekly Leak Check are on by default. Two-factor login is available but each person turns it on for themselves. CAPTCHA, the honeypot, the breached-password check and the hardening options are off until you switch them on."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:750
msgid "Authlify creates three database tables (activity log, lockout counters and passkeys) and a daily clean-up task."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:751
#, php-format
msgid "On a site upgraded from Modify Login 1.x or 2.x, the old login address, redirects and log carry over, and new protection starts switched off. See %s."
