msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:885
#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1616
msgid "How to hide your login page safely"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:889
msgid "Getting back in (recovery)"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:889
msgid "Every way to recover a forgotten login address or get past a lockout, without FTP support tickets."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:891
#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1682
msgid "Forgot the login address"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:892
msgid "<strong>Email.</strong> Each time the address changes, Authlify emails it to the site admin address and to the person who changed it. Search your mail for “Your login address”. While logged in, <strong>Login URL → If you ever lose the login URL → Email it to me now</strong> sends it again."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:893
msgid "<strong>wp-config.php.</strong> Add this line above “That’s all, stop editing!”. The custom address is switched off and wp-login.php works again. Remove the line afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:894
msgid "<strong>WP-CLI.</strong> Show the address, or turn the custom address off:"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:896
msgid "Force a known address"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:896
msgid "To set the address from wp-config.php instead (for example on a staging copy), define <code>AUTHLIFY_SLUG</code>. It must be 3 to 64 lowercase letters, numbers, hyphens or underscores and not a reserved word; an invalid value is ignored. While the constant is set, the Login URL field is locked and <code>wp authlify url set</code> refuses to run."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:896
msgid "If both constants are set, <code>AUTHLIFY_DISABLE_HIDE</code> wins. <code>wp authlify url reset</code> cannot override <code>AUTHLIFY_SLUG</code>; remove the constant instead."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:897
msgid "Locked out after wrong passwords"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:898
msgid "Wait: the lockout message says how long. The first lockout lasts 15 minutes by default."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:899
msgid "Click <strong>“Is this your account? Email me an unlock link.”</strong> under the lockout message. The link arrives at the account’s own email address and works for 30 minutes. It lets that one account log in from the same IP address; the lockout for everyone else stays. At most three requests per hour per address."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:900
msgid "Another administrator can unlock you under <strong>Security → Brute force → Locked out right now</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:901
msgid "With WP-CLI:"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:903
msgid "Blocked by CAPTCHA or two-factor"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:903
